-- title:
--   Local constancy of μ(h) on small chordal balls, uniformly in μ
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and work with $\overline F_N :=$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, the subfield of the Laurent series field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the images of the level-$N$ modular function field. Let $r \in \mathbb N$ and let $s : \mathrm{Fin}\,r \to \overline F_N$ satisfy `IsEmbBasis N s`, i.e. $s$ is linearly independent over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and its range spans the Riemann–Roch space $\{f : \mathrm{ord}_v(f) \ge -D(v) \text{ for all } v\}$ of the divisor `embDivisor N` $=$ `embDegree N` times the cusp at infinity. Let $h \in \overline F_N$, let $Q$ be a place of $\overline F_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (a proper valuation subring containing the base field, with principal ideals) such that $\mathrm{ord}_Q(h) = 0$, and let $p$ be a prime. Then there exists a real $c \ge 0$ with the following property: for every non-archimedean absolute value $\mu$ on $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\mu(p) < 1$, and every place $R$ of $\overline F_N$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\mathrm{ord}_R(h) = 0$, if
--   $$c\,\bigl(-\log \mu(p)\bigr) \;\le\; \log \sup_i \mu(x_i) + \log \sup_j \mu(y_j) - \log \sup_{i,j} \mu(x_i y_j - x_j y_i),$$
--   where $x =$ `evalVec s R` and $y =$ `evalVec s Q` are the pivot-normalised coordinate rows $i \mapsto v.\mathrm{evalAt}\bigl(s_i \cdot s_{\mathrm{pivotIndex}(s,v)}^{-1}\bigr)$ (the pivot being an index minimising $\mathrm{ord}_v \circ s$; the row is $0$ when $r = 0$), then $\mu\bigl(\mathrm{evalAt}_R(h)\bigr) = \mu\bigl(\mathrm{evalAt}_Q(h)\bigr)$, the evaluations being taken through a chosen section of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ residue field.
--
--   This is the local-constancy step in the chordal-proximity analysis of the modular curve $X_0(N)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$: a function that is a unit at a fixed place $Q$ has constant $\mu$-absolute value on the chordal ball of radius $e^{-c(-\log\mu(p))}$ about $Q$, with the constant $c$ depending only on $s$, $h$, $Q$ and $p$ and hence uniform over all non-archimedean $\mu$ lying over $p$. It feeds the lower bound for $\log\mu$ of an evaluation under a proximity hypothesis, [`ModularCurve.exists_log_absValue_evalAt_ge_of_forall_prox_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_log_absValue_evalAt_ge_of_forall_prox_le).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZero_exists_abv_evalAt_eq_abv_evalAt_of_le_prox.lean

